<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47863" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾰνάσῐμος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>deadly,
			fatal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				610e
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1276
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέσημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					1033
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείρωμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OT</u>
					560
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					758
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάρμακα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					616
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				103.31
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
				53
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρία θ</span>., of
				<i>poisonous</i> reptiles, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.56.4
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θανάσιμα, τά</span>, <i>poisons,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Marc.
				16.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.108
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.154
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως, τύπτειν</span> to strike <i>with
				deadly blow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				4.3.4
			</span></i>: neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίδες -μα δάκνουσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.87
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>belonging to death</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ.
			αἷμα</span> the <i>life</i>-blood, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1019
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλψασα θ. γόον</span>
			having sung her <i>death</i>-song, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1445
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐκπνοαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1438
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>near death</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				819
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἤδη ὄντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					408b
				</span></i>
			; <i>liable to the death-penalty,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Abh.Berl.Akad.
				1925(5).21
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyrene</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>dead</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				517
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. βεβηκότα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OT</u>
					959
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
